body:
Hi @safeimuslim and thanks for opening this issue.

From [StackOverflow](https://stackoverflow.com/a/48579915/654253):

The infiniteHits has very little logic in it. Here is what I'll do:

```javascript
    // custom widget
    var customInfiniteHits = instantsearch.connectors.connectInfiniteHits(function(options, isFirstRendering) {
      var showMore = options.showMore;
      var hits = options.hits;
      var containerNode = otpions.widgetParams.containerNode;
    
      if(isFirstRendering) {
        bindScroll(showMore);
      }
    
      containerNode.html(
        hits.map(function(hit) {
          return '<div>' + hit._highlightResult.name.value + '</div>';
        })
      );
    });
    
    // Usage
    search.addWidget(
      customInfiniteHits({
        containerNode: $('#custom-infinite-hits-container'),
      })
    );
```

`bindScroll` is the function that will listen to scroll position and will call the `showMore` provided. This function does not take parameters.
